Subject: pin by default: no unload without unload=allowed

C3-1 section 2: _unload is called only when the module declares
unload=allowed and nothing holds it.  The .moddata parser read the key
but nothing used it, so moduload unloaded any idle module.  The record
now carries DM_UNLOADOK from unload=allowed; dlm_unload refuses a pinned
module with EBUSY (moduload(0) leaves it), and modstat reports it locked.
The state harness's modules declare unload=allowed, since it unloads
them; pin1 declares nothing and is refused (amix-dlm 30 section 2, patch
14 of the plan's numbering).

--- a/dlm.h
+++ b/dlm.h
@@ -223,6 +223,7 @@
 #define	DM_LOCKED	0x10	/* profiler */
 #define	DM_SYMOK	0x20	/* table usable */
 #define	DM_WANTED	0x40	/* someone sleeps on the record */
+#define	DM_UNLOADOK	0x80	/* .moddata unload=allowed; else pinned */
 #define	DM_TRANS	(DM_LOADING | DM_UNLOADING)
 
 /* dlm_load() flags */
--- a/dlm_core.c
+++ b/dlm_core.c
@@ -781,6 +781,8 @@
